#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0123.1 expect=noViolation domain=SE
#note "Authority: SEND Conformance Rules v5.0 SEND123.1, Condition 'Element occurs that is not one of the planned elements', Rule 'ETCD = UNPLAN'; Plain Text: 'If a particular period of time cannot be represented as one of the planned Elements, then UNPLAN is used as the value for ETCD and ELEMENT is left blank'. Partially Executable (Overreporting): the Check cannot tell an unplanned element from a mis-coded planned one, and does not test the companion 'ELEMENT is left blank'; so every UNPLAN row here keeps ELEMENT blank, and the flagged row is unambiguously an element outside the plan (its ELEMENT names no TE element). Rows 1, 2 and 4 carry planned TE element codes (SCRN, TRT, RECOV); row 3 is an unplanned period coded ETCD=UNPLAN with ELEMENT blank, exactly as the authority prescribes -> silent."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 0
dataset SE label="Subject Elements"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SESEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col ETCD    type=Char label="Element Code"
col ELEMENT type=Char label="Description of Element"
col SESTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Element"
---
S1 | SE | S1-001 | 1 | SCRN   | Screening | 2024-01-01
S1 | SE | S1-001 | 2 | TRT    | Treatment | 2024-01-08
S1 | SE | S1-001 | 3 | UNPLAN |           | 2024-02-05
S1 | SE | S1-001 | 4 | RECOV  | Recovery  | 2024-02-12
---

dataset TE label="Trial Elements"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col ETCD    type=Char label="Element Code"
col ELEMENT type=Char label="Description of Element"
col TESTRL  type=Char label="Rule for Start of Element"
---
S1 | TE | SCRN  | Screening | First day of acclimation
S1 | TE | TRT   | Treatment | First dose
S1 | TE | RECOV | Recovery  | Day after last dose
---
